{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And there came out fire from before HaShem and consumed upon the altar.</b> Behold now, on the eighth day, when the Tabernacle was consecrated with the aforementioned offerings brought to atone for the sin of the calf, fire came down from heaven to receive them. And this is the fire that endured until the generation of Solomon, who built the House; all the days of the House the fire existed, it did not go out until it was destroyed. And concerning this the verse hinted (Leviticus 6:6): ״אש תמיד תוקד על המזבח לא תכבה״. And likewise we find twelve fires that fell from heaven in different generations and times: six of them were to receive the offerings, in a manner of acceptance and compassion, and the remaining six in a manner of anger and vengeance. <b>The first</b> is this fire that came down to receive these offerings with which the Tabernacle was consecrated, concerning which it is written: ״ותצא אש מלפני ה' ותאכל על המזבח את העולה ואת החלבים״. <b>The second</b> is the one that came down in the days of Gideon when he asked a sign from the angel, as it is written (Judges 6:17–18): ״ועשית לי אות שאתה מדבר עמי״, ״אל נא תמוש מזה עד באי אליך״, and it is written: ״וגדעון בא ויעש גדי עזים״, and it is written: ״ויגע בבשר ובמצות ותעל האש מן הצור״. And because He commanded him to do five things, he asked Him for a sign so that the matter might be verified in his heart: first He said to him, ״קח את פר השור אשר לאביך״ — that is, take it for yourself, and the intention is that he should uproot it from the world so that it not be worshipped; and ״פר השני שבע שנים״ — meaning the second-born to the womb; ״והרסת את מזבח הבעל אשר לאביך ואת האשרה אשר עליו תכרות״; ״ובנית מזבח לה' אלהיך על ראש המעוז הזה במערכה״ — and the meaning of המעוז is a hard, rocky mountain, from the same root as עזאזל; and because of this he needed a sign in order to do these things. And <b>the third</b> is the fire that came down in the days of Manoah when the angel revealed himself to his wife, and it is written (Judges 13): ״אם תעצרני לא אוכל בלחמך״ etc., and it is written: ״ויקח מנוח את גדי העזים ואת המנחה ויעל על הצור לה'״, and it is written: ״ויהי כעלות הלהב מעל המזבח השמימה״. Our Rabbi Saadia, of blessed memory, explained that at first he called the mountain צור — ״ויעל על הצור״ — and after the offering was accepted he called it מזבח; and the sign was for Manoah and his wife in order that the words of the angel concerning the son he had announced to them might be verified in their hearts. And <b>the fourth</b> was in the days of David, when the plague came upon the people and David purchased the place at the threshing floor of Araunah the Jebusite, and it is written (1 Chronicles 21:26): ״ויבן שם דויד מזבח לה' ויעל עולות ושלמים ויקרא אל ה' ויענהו באש מן השמים על מזבח העולה״. And <b>the fifth</b> was in the days of Solomon, when the building of the Holy Temple was completed, as it is written (2 Chronicles 7:1): ״וככלות שלמה להתפלל והאש ירדה מן השמים ותאכל העולה והזבחים וכבוד ה' מלא את הבית״. And if a questioner should ask: why was this fire necessary, since the fire that came down in the days of Moses was already there? And the answer is that the bronze altar could not contain the offerings of Solomon's time because of their multitude, and most of them were offered in the court; that is what is written (1 Kings 8:64): ״ביום ההוא קדש המלך את תוך החצר״, and it explained the reason, and said: ״כי מזבח הנחשת אשר לפני ה' קטן מהכיל את העולה ואת המנחה״. And they were not permitted to bring fire from outside into the court, for it would be strange fire; nor were they permitted to take fire from upon the bronze altar and carry it out into the court, for they would profane it — and one does not degrade consecrated things, and it may not be taken down; and therefore the Holy Temple needed this sign, that fire should come down from heaven into the court. And <b>the sixth</b> was in the days of Elijah, that is what is written (1 Kings 18): ״ענני ה' ענני״ — the first, for the descent of the fire; the second, for the descent of the rain — because he had sworn (1 Kings 17): ״אם יהיה השנים האלה טל ומטר״ etc. Or it means to say: ״ענני״ — the first, that fire should come down and receive the offerings; ״ענני״ — the second, with addition and increase of the fire, so that the waters would not be able to extinguish it but it would lick up the waters, in the manner of what is written (1 Kings 18): ״ואת המים אשר בתעלה לחכה״." "<b>And in Berakhot</b> chapter one: ״ענני ה'״ — R. Ammi said: ״ענני״ — that fire should come down from heaven and consume them; ״ענני״ — that He should divert their attention, so they would not say, ״These are the deeds of vanity, they are the deeds of sorcery.״ And the six that came down in a manner of anger and vengeance: <b>the first</b> is this fire upon Nadab and Abihu, that is what is written (Leviticus 10): ״ותצא אש מלפני ה'״ etc. <b>The second</b>, when the people complained against Moses (Numbers 11): ״ויהי העם כמתאוננים רע״, and it is written: ״ותבער בם אש ה'״. <b>The third</b>, in the dispute of Korah, as it is written (Numbers 16): ״ואש יצאה מאת ה' ותאכל את החמשים ומאתים איש״. <b>The fourth</b>, in the matter of Job, as it is said (Job 1): ״אש האלהים נפלה מן השמים״. <b>The fifth and the sixth</b>, both through Elijah: fire came down from heaven and consumed the captain of fifty and his men, and a second time fire came down and consumed the second captain of fifty and his men; that is what is written (2 Kings 1): ״ותרד אש מן השמים ותאכל אותו ואת חמשיו״. And both were punished because they spoke to Elijah with pride and greatness of heart — the first said (there): ״המלך דבר רדה״, and the second said (there): ״כה אמר המלך מהרה רדה״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {1 "Citation reads 'ובברכות פרק קמא' — 'and in Berakhot chapter one'; the Gemara passage (Berakhot 9b) that comments on Elijah's ענני is found at the end of chapter 1 of tractate Berakhot."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:43.980672797Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}